Hi,

I'm getting the same error message as Giacomo:
model3 <- oSCR.fit(model = list(D ~ 1, # model describing variation pixel density (D(si))
p0 ~ offset(log.effort) + placement, # model describing variation in baseline encounter prob/rate (p0)  sig ~ 1), # model describing variation in sigma (space use)  encmod = "P",  scrFrame = reduced.cheetah, # the scrFrame object  ssDF = state.space.cheetah) #, # the ssDF object Fitting model: D~1, p0~placement + offset(log.effort), sigma~1, asu~1 Using ll function 'msLL.nosex' Hold on tight! 2025-01-10 16:06:02.521526 p0.(Intercept) | sig.(Intercept) | t.beta.placementrandom | t.beta.placementtrail | t.beta.placementwaterhole | d0.(Intercept) | Error in solve.default(myfit$hessian) : Lapack routine dgesv: system is exactly singular: U[3,3] = 0

I am estimating cheetah abundance from camera trapping data. The problem might be from the covariate placement (which is a factorial covariate indicating whether each camera is placed by a playing tree, water hole, trail or in a riverbank), as the error only occurs when I include this covariate. I tried to reduce the buffer of the SSDF and the error message changes to a warning message:

model3 <- oSCR.fit(model = list(D ~ 1, # model describing variation pixel density (D(si))  p0 ~ offset(log.effort) + placement, # model describing variation in baseline encounter prob/rate (p0)  sig ~ 1), # model describing variation in sigma (space use)  encmod = "P",  scrFrame = reduced.cheetah, # the scrFrame object  ssDF = state.space.cheetah) ) #, # the ssDF object Fitting model: D~1, p0~placement + offset(log.effort), sigma~1, asu~1 Using ll function 'msLL.nosex' Hold on tight! 2025-01-10 16:27:40.604548 p0.(Intercept) | sig.(Intercept) | t.beta.placementrandom | t.beta.placementtrail | t.beta.placementwaterhole | d0.(Intercept) |  Model: D ~ 1 p0 ~ offset(log.effort) + placement sig ~ 1 Run time: 7.565 minutes AIC: 170.6243 Summary table: Estimate SE z P(>|z|) p0.(Intercept) -5.836 0.374 -15.613 0.000 t.beta.placementrandom -21.452 NaN NaN NaN t.beta.placementtrail -1.913 0.660 -2.898 0.004 t.beta.placementwaterhole 1.042 0.471 2.212 0.027 sig.(Intercept) 9.193 0.197 46.683 0.000 d0.(Intercept) -5.736 0.352 -16.304 0.000 *Density intercept is log(individuals per pixel) Nhat(state-space) = exp(d0.)*nrow(ssDF) (caution is warranted when model contains density covariates) Warning message: In sqrt(diag(solve(myfit$hessian))) : NaNs produced

Do you have any thoughts on how I can fix this issue?

Thanks a lot for your help.
Filipe Rocha

