Hi Asia,

I’m sorry for the confusion, but collared individuals can have >1 capture. The index in “cap.tel <http://cap.tel>” is the row of the capture history matrix/array that contains the trap captures for each collared individual, however many there are. This lets the model code line up the likelihood of the telemetry locations with the correct likelihood of trap captures.

Happy to help further!

